[For "white"]
[Kind "sideline"]
[Start "caro-w-nf6-qc7 6.Qb3"]
[Name "4...Nf6 5.c3 Bg4: 6...b6"]

6... b6 { Keeps the pawn safe from the queen, and leaves c6 weak. }
7. Bf4 { The bishop comes out as usual. }
7... e6
8. Nd2 { The usual knight. If 8...Nc6, Bb5 wins a piece, as in the line with 7...b6. }
8... Bd6
( 8... Nc6? { A natural move, but this is the position of the line with 7...b6, and the knight has walked into the pin. }
  9. Bb5 { Pins the knight to the king, and the pawn on e6 stops the bishop on g4 from getting back to d7. [%idea pin] }
  9... Rc8
  10. Qa4 Qd7
  11. Ngf3 { Ne5 comes next, and three attackers against two guards win the knight on c6. } )
9. Bxd6 Qxd6
10. Ngf3 { Develops. White has a small edge: the pawn on b6 has left c6 and the light squares weak. White castles next. } *
